{
  "_comment": "Bulk coverage to fill the 2 TB. Global z9-13 gives every user regional through town-level detail, which today exists only for Iberia. z14 over the populated continents adds street level on top. Antarctica is deliberately absent: at 47.9M tiles it is the single most expensive region on earth, because Mercator tiles cover almost no ground at that latitude, and it has no users.",
